These are also different.

1) SecurityContext
Defined in the Pod/Container specification.
For example:
securityContext:
  runAsNonRoot: true

It says:
This Pod/container should run as non-root.

2) SCC
OpenShift checks whether that security configuration is permitted.
So:
Deployment YAML
       │
       ▼
securityContext
       │
       ▼
     SCC
       │
       ▼
Allowed / Rejected


